## Defect 1: Cleanup only runs when presenting — breaks non-presenting workloads

**File:** `src/gpu/vulkan/SDL_gpu_vulkan.c`  
**Lines:** ~10529-10570 (in the `VULKAN_Submit` function)

**Failure scenario:** Any GPU workload that doesn't present to a swapchain (compute-only dispatches, headless rendering, offscreen render-to-texture, compute shaders) will **never clean up submitted command buffers, never deallocate empty memory allocations, and never process pending destroys**. Resources leak indefinitely → OOM or crash.

**Evidence from diff:** The old code (lines 10467-10508 in original) ran cleanup unconditionally:
```c
// Check if we can perform any cleanups
for (Sint32 i = renderer->submittedCommandBufferCount - 1; i >= 0; i -= 1) { ... }
if (renderer->checkEmptyAllocations) { ... }
VULKAN_INTERNAL_PerformPendingDestroys(renderer);
// Defrag! (only if presenting)
```

The new code (lines 10529-10570) wraps **all** cleanup inside `if (presenting)`:
```c
// If presenting, check if we can perform any cleanups
if (presenting) {
    for (Sint32 i = ...) { ... }
    if (renderer->checkEmptyAllocations) { ... }
    VULKAN_INTERNAL_PerformPendingDestroys(renderer);
}
```

`presenting` is set at line 10421: `bool presenting = vulkanCommandBuffer->presentDataCount > 0;` — so compute-only command buffers (presentDataCount == 0) skip all cleanup.

